# Field

Lays out form controls with their labels, descriptions, and errors. Combine it with any control, such as `Input`, `Textarea`, `Checkbox`, `Switch`, or `RadioGroup`. For validation, use the `form` item, which builds on these parts.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Field, FieldSet, FieldLegend, FieldGroup, FieldLabel, FieldDescription } from "#lib/components/ui/field/index.js";
	import { Input } from "#lib/components/ui/input/index.js";
</script>

<FieldSet>
	<FieldLegend>Payment method</FieldLegend>
	<FieldDescription>All transactions are secure and encrypted.</FieldDescription>
	<FieldGroup>
		<Field>
			<FieldLabel for="card-name">Name on card</FieldLabel>
			<Input id="card-name" placeholder="Evil Rabbit" />
		</Field>
		<Field>
			<FieldLabel for="card-number">Card number</FieldLabel>
			<Input id="card-number" aria-describedby="card-number-description" />
			<FieldDescription id="card-number-description">Enter your 16-digit card number.</FieldDescription>
		</Field>
	</FieldGroup>
</FieldSet>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/field.json
```

## Anatomy

`Field` renders a `div` with `role="group"` that holds one control with its `FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, and `FieldError`. `FieldGroup` stacks fields with a larger gap. `FieldSet` and `FieldLegend` render a `fieldset` and `legend` for related fields, such as an address. `FieldContent` holds the label and description beside a control in a horizontal field.

Link each label to its control with `for` and a matching `id`, and the description with `aria-describedby`.

## Horizontal

Set `orientation="horizontal"` to place the control beside its label, such as a checkbox or a switch. Wrap the label and description in `FieldContent` so they stack. Set `orientation="responsive"` to stack on narrow screens and switch to a row once the `FieldGroup` is `28rem` wide; the group is a container, so it measures its own width instead of the viewport.

<Demo section="horizontal" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Field orientation="horizontal">
	<Checkbox id="terms" />
	<FieldLabel for="terms">Accept terms and conditions</FieldLabel>
</Field>
<Field orientation="horizontal">
	<FieldContent>
		<FieldLabel for="marketing">Marketing emails</FieldLabel>
		<FieldDescription>Receive emails about new products and features.</FieldDescription>
	</FieldContent>
	<Switch id="marketing" />
</Field>
```

## Choice cards

Wrap a whole `Field` in `FieldLabel` to turn it into a selectable card. The card highlights while the checkbox, radio, or switch inside it is checked. Use `FieldTitle` for the heading inside the card, since the card is already the label. Set `variant="label"` on `FieldLegend` to shrink it to the label size above a set of cards.

<Demo section="choice" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<RadioGroup defaultValue="kubernetes">
	<FieldLabel for="kubernetes">
		<Field orientation="horizontal">
			<FieldContent>
				<FieldTitle>Kubernetes</FieldTitle>
				<FieldDescription>Run GPU workloads on a cluster.</FieldDescription>
			</FieldContent>
			<RadioGroupItem value="kubernetes" id="kubernetes" />
		</Field>
	</FieldLabel>
</RadioGroup>
```

## Errors

Set `invalid` on `Field` to turn its label destructive, and pass `errors` to `FieldError`, such as zod issues. One message shows as text and several as a list, with repeated messages shown once. `FieldError` renders `role="alert"`, so screen readers announce it, and renders nothing without errors. Set `aria-invalid="true"` on the control for its invalid ring.

<Demo section="error" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Field invalid>
	<FieldLabel for="username">Username</FieldLabel>
	<Input id="username" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="username-error" />
	<FieldError id="username-error" errors={[{ message: "Username must be at least 3 characters." }]} />
</Field>
```

## Disabled

Set `disabled` on `Field` to dim its label and description beside a disabled control.

<Demo section="disabled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Field disabled>
	<FieldLabel for="team">Team name</FieldLabel>
	<Input id="team" value="Acme" disabled aria-describedby="team-description" />
	<FieldDescription id="team-description">Only owners can rename the team.</FieldDescription>
</Field>
```

## Separator

Place `FieldSeparator` between sections. Pass text to show it in the middle of the line.

<Demo section="separator" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<FieldSeparator>Or continue with</FieldSeparator>
```

## API

`Field`, `FieldGroup`, `FieldContent`, `FieldTitle`, and `FieldSeparator` extend the native `div` attributes. `FieldSet`, `FieldLegend`, `FieldLabel`, and `FieldDescription` extend the `fieldset`, `legend`, `label`, and `p` attributes. The parts have no `size`; size the controls inside them instead.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** `vertical` stacks the label above the control; `horizontal` places them side by side; `responsive` switches to a row when the `FieldGroup` is wide enough; defaults to `vertical` */
	orientation?: "vertical" | "horizontal" | "responsive";
	/** Colors the label and error in the destructive color */
	invalid?: boolean;
	/** Dims the label and description */
	disabled?: boolean;
}

interface LegendProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"legend"> {
	/** `legend` is a section heading; `label` matches the field label size */
	variant?: "legend" | "label";
}

interface ErrorProps extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Errors to list, such as zod issues; repeated messages are shown once */
	errors?: ({ message?: string } | undefined)[];
	/** Custom error content in place of `errors` */
	children?: Snippet;
}
```
